### Find Row with Maximum 1s

Given a binary matrix where each row is sorted in non-decreasing order, find the index of the row containing the maximum number of 1s.

Since the rows are sorted, I used Binary Search to find the first occurrence of 1 in each row. Once the first 1 is found, the number of 1s in that row can be calculated as:

Number of 1s = Total columns - Index of first 1

I keep track of the row with the maximum number of 1s and return its index.

**Time Complexity:** O(rows × log(columns))  
**Space Complexity:** O(1)

###Solution

class Solution {
    public int rowWithMax1s(int[][] mat) {
       int max=0;
       int index=-1;
       for(int i=0;i<mat.length;i++)
       {
        int first=lowerbound(mat[i],mat[0].length,1);
        int count=mat[0].length-first;
        if(count>max)
        {
            max=count;
            index=i;
        }
       }
       return index;
    }
    static public int lowerbound(int[] arr,int n,int x)
    {
        int low=0,high=n-1;
        int ans=n;
        while(low<=high)
        {
            int mid=low+(high-low)/2;
            if(arr[mid]>=x)
            {
                ans=mid;
                high=mid-1;
            }
            else low=mid+1;
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
